//@version=6

//@description Shared pivot structure outline helpers for MYNAMEISBRANDON Pine scripts.

library("PivotStructureOutline_Utilities", true)

// 4-27-2026 - no changes to script, just adding new chart that shows new anchored vwap helpers.
//The new helpers are designed for scripts that already resolve active pivot structure anchors and want a reusable way to draw anchored VWAP paths from those anchors.
//This expands the library beyond outline lines, anchor boxes, and active anchor markers into a broader pivot-structure visual framework. A script can now use the same resolved high-side / low-side anchors that feed its outline or anchor boxes to also build pivot-anchored AVWAP paths.
//The library remains engine-agnostic. It does not confirm pivots, choose active anchors, decide which side should display, or define a script’s AVWAP styling. The calling script still controls the pivot engine, anchor model, visibility logic, colors, line widths, and whether it wants to display pivot-bar AVWAPs, confirmation-bar AVWAPs, or both.

// ==============================================================================================
// 📚 LIBRARY MAP
// ==============================================================================================
//
// PivotStructureOutline_Utilities is currently organized into:
//
// • Outline Line Style Helpers
// • Pivot Structure Outline Helpers
// • Pivot Structure Anchor Resolution Helpers
// • Pivot Structure Anchor Array Helpers
// • Pivot Structure Anchor Box Helpers
// • Active Anchor Marker Helpers
// • Pivot Structure AVWAP Helpers
// • Line Object Helpers
// • Box Object Helpers
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Outline Line Style Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable line-style resolution for outline-driven line objects.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     This region helps scripts:
//
//     • convert a simple UI string into a Pine line style enum
//     • reuse one consistent style resolver across:
//          top outline line
//          bottom outline line
//          left top connector
//          left bottom connector
//          midpoint line
//
// 🧰 OUTPUT OPTIONS:
//     • line.style_solid
//     • line.style_dashed
//     • line.style_dotted
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Outline Line Style Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Converts a string input into the matching Pine line style.
//
// Behavior:
//     • "Solid"  -> line.style_solid
//     • "Dashed" -> line.style_dashed
//     • fallback -> line.style_dotted
//
// Notes:
//     • Good fit for scripts that keep style inputs at script level
//     • This helper only resolves style
//     • Line object lifecycle can remain script-level or be handled through
//       outlineManageLine()
//

// @function Resolves a Pine line style from a string input
// @param styleIn Style string. Expected values: "Solid", "Dashed", or "Dotted"
// @returns Pine line style enum
export outlineLineStyle(simple string styleIn) =>
    styleIn == "Solid" ? line.style_solid :
     styleIn == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed :
     line.style_dotted

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// import MYNAMEISBRANDON/PivotStructureOutline_Utilities/3 as PSOutils
//
// outlineMainStyle = PSOutils.outlineLineStyle("Dotted")

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Outline Line Style Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Pivot Structure Outline Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable helpers for building a pivot structure outline framework
//     from already-confirmed high / low pivot anchors.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     This region helps scripts:
//
//     • resolve a pivot-close anchor from a confirmed pivot index
//     • choose whether the outline top/bottom should append to wick anchors or close anchors
//     • build the live geometry needed for:
//          top outline span
//          bottom outline span
//          midpoint line
//          left top connector
//          left bottom connector
//
// 📘 INTERPRETATION:
//     • This library is engine-agnostic.
//     • It does not care whether the confirmed pivots came from:
//          price pivots
//          oscillator pivots
//          or another confirmed-pivot engine
//     • The calling script is responsible for supplying already-resolved:
//          confirmed pivot indexes
//          wick anchors
//          close anchors
//
// 🧰 OUTPUT OPTIONS:
//     • Confirmed pivot close value
//     • Selected high / low outline anchors
//     • Live top / bottom / midpoint levels
//     • Left / right x coordinates
//     • Midpoint start x
//     • Left top connector source
//     • Left bottom connector source
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Pivot Close Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Returns the close value belonging to an already-confirmed pivot index.
//
// Behavior:
//     • Converts pivotIdx into bars-back distance from the current bar
//     • Returns close[barsBack] when the pivot index is valid
//     • Returns na when the pivot index cannot be resolved safely
//
// Notes:
//     • Good fit for scripts that already maintain generic confirmed pivot indexes
//     • This keeps the library independent from the pivot-engine internals
//

// @function Returns the close value belonging to a confirmed pivot index
// @param pivotIdx Confirmed pivot bar_index
// @param closeValue Close series
// @returns Confirmed pivot close value
export outlinePivotCloseFromIdx(
     int pivotIdx,
     float closeValue) =>

    int barsBack =
         not na(pivotIdx) ? bar_index - pivotIdx : na

    not na(barsBack) and barsBack >= 0 ? closeValue[barsBack] : na


// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Outline Anchor Selector
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Selects the high and low outline anchors from Wick or Close mode.
//
// Behavior:
//     • "Wick"  -> uses the supplied wick anchors
//     • "Close" -> uses the supplied close anchors
//     • Returns an outline-valid state when both selected anchors exist
//
// Notes:
//     • Good fit for scripts that store:
//          lastHighPivotPrice
//          lastLowPivotPrice
//          lastHighPivotClose
//          lastLowPivotClose
//

// @function Selects the active outline anchors from Wick or Close mode
// @param anchorMode Anchor mode. Expected values: "Wick" or "Close"
// @param highWickAnchor Confirmed high-side wick anchor
// @param lowWickAnchor Confirmed low-side wick anchor
// @param highCloseAnchor Confirmed high-side close anchor
// @param lowCloseAnchor Confirmed low-side close anchor
// @returns Selected high anchor, selected low anchor, is outline-valid
export outlineSelectedAnchors(
     simple string anchorMode,
     float highWickAnchor,
     float lowWickAnchor,
     float highCloseAnchor,
     float lowCloseAnchor) =>

    bool useCloseAnchors =
         anchorMode == "Close"

    float highAnchor =
         useCloseAnchors ? highCloseAnchor : highWickAnchor

    float lowAnchor =
         useCloseAnchors ? lowCloseAnchor : lowWickAnchor

    bool ok =
         not na(highAnchor) and
         not na(lowAnchor)

    [highAnchor, lowAnchor, ok]


// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Outline Geometry Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Builds the live geometry used by the pivot structure outline system.
//
// Behavior:
//     • Uses the confirmed high-pivot index and low-pivot index as the two anchor bars
//     • The earlier pivot bar becomes the shared left-edge source bar
//     • The right edge always extends to the current bar
//     • The midpoint is calculated from the selected high and low anchors
//     • Midline start mode controls where the midpoint line begins:
//
//          "Most Recent Pivot":
//              midpoint line starts at the later of the two confirmed pivot bars
//
//          "Left Outline":
//              midpoint line starts at the shared left outline edge
//
//     • Connector source mode controls how the connectors touch the left bar:
//
//          "Wick":
//              left top connector source    = high[left bar]
//              left bottom connector source = low[left bar]
//
//          "Close":
//              left top connector source    = close[left bar]
//              left bottom connector source = close[left bar]
//
// Notes:
//     • This helper returns geometry only
//     • Colors, widths, visibility toggles, and render order remain script-level
//     • This allows scripts to keep the current midpoint behavior as the default
//       while optionally letting users extend the midpoint all the way to the
//       left outline edge
//     • Line lifecycle can remain script-level or be handled through
//       outlineManageLine()
//

// @function Returns the live geometry for the pivot structure outline system
// @param highPivotIdx Confirmed high pivot bar_index
// @param lowPivotIdx Confirmed low pivot bar_index
// @param highAnchor Selected top outline anchor
// @param lowAnchor Selected bottom outline anchor
// @param connectorSourceMode Connector source mode. Expected values: "Wick" or "Close"
// @param midlineStartMode Midline start mode. Expected values: "Most Recent Pivot" or "Left Outline"
// @param highValue High series
// @param lowValue Low series
// @param closeValue Close series
// @returns ok, leftX, rightX, midX1, topY, bottomY, midY, leftTopConnectorY, leftBottomConnectorY
export outlineGeometry(
     int highPivotIdx,
     int lowPivotIdx,
     float highAnchor,
     float lowAnchor,
     simple string connectorSourceMode,
     simple string midlineStartMode,
     float highValue,
     float lowValue,
     float closeValue) =>

    bool ok =
         not na(highPivotIdx) and
         not na(lowPivotIdx) and
         not na(highAnchor) and
         not na(lowAnchor)

    int leftX =
         ok ? math.min(highPivotIdx, lowPivotIdx) : na

    int rightX =
         ok ? bar_index : na

    int laterPivotX =
         ok ? math.max(highPivotIdx, lowPivotIdx) : na

    int midX1 =
         ok ? (midlineStartMode == "Left Outline" ? leftX : laterPivotX) : na

    int leftBA =
         ok ? bar_index - leftX : na

    bool useCloseConnectorSource =
         connectorSourceMode == "Close"

    float topY =
         ok ? highAnchor : na

    float bottomY =
         ok ? lowAnchor : na

    float midY =
         ok ? (highAnchor + lowAnchor) / 2.0 : na

    float leftTopConnectorY =
         ok and not na(leftBA) and leftBA >= 0 ?
         (useCloseConnectorSource ? closeValue[leftBA] : highValue[leftBA]) :
         na

    float leftBottomConnectorY =
         ok and not na(leftBA) and leftBA >= 0 ?
         (useCloseConnectorSource ? closeValue[leftBA] : lowValue[leftBA]) :
         na

    [ok, leftX, rightX, midX1, topY, bottomY, midY, leftTopConnectorY, leftBottomConnectorY]


// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example usage in a script that imports this library:
//
// import MYNAMEISBRANDON/PivotStructureOutline_Utilities/3 as PSOutils
//
// var float lastHighPivotClose = na
// var float lastLowPivotClose = na
//
// if highConfirmed and not na(highPivotIdx)
//     lastHighPivotClose := PSOutils.outlinePivotCloseFromIdx(
//          highPivotIdx,
//          close)
//
// if lowConfirmed and not na(lowPivotIdx)
//     lastLowPivotClose := PSOutils.outlinePivotCloseFromIdx(
//          lowPivotIdx,
//          close)
//
// [outlineHighAnchor, outlineLowAnchor, outlineAnchorsOk] = PSOutils.outlineSelectedAnchors(
//      in_zigLookbackOutlineAppendTo,
//      lastHighPivotPrice,
//      lastLowPivotPrice,
//      lastHighPivotClose,
//      lastLowPivotClose)
//
// [outlineOk, outlineLeftX, outlineRightX, outlineMidX1, outlineTopY, outlineBottomY, outlineMidY, outlineLeftTopConnectorY, outlineLeftBottomConnectorY] = PSOutils.outlineGeometry(
//      lastHighPivotIdx,
//      lastLowPivotIdx,
//      outlineHighAnchor,
//      outlineLowAnchor,
//      "Wick",
//      "Most Recent Pivot",
//      high,
//      low,
//      close)
//
// outlineMainStyle = PSOutils.outlineLineStyle(in_zigLookbackOutlineStyle)
// outlineMidStyle = PSOutils.outlineLineStyle(in_zigLookbackOutlineMidlineStyle)

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Pivot Structure Outline Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Pivot Structure Anchor Resolution Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable helpers for resolving the active structure anchor from a
//     small rolling set of already-confirmed pivot records.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     This region helps scripts:
//
//     • keep confirmed-pivot memory script-level
//     • pass the most recent 1, 2, 3, or 4 same-side pivot records into a resolver
//     • select the highest high-side anchor from the requested lookback
//     • select the lowest low-side anchor from the requested lookback
//     • carry the selected anchor's matching close, auxiliary value, pivot index,
//       and confirmation index forward with the selected price
//
// 📘 INTERPRETATION:
//     • This helper is engine-agnostic.
//     • It does not confirm pivots.
//     • It does not store pivot memory.
//     • It only chooses the active anchor from pivot records supplied by the script.
//     • The auxiliary value can be RSI, another oscillator, a score, or any other
//       value the script wants to keep attached to the selected anchor.
//
// ==============================================================================================

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: High-Side Anchor Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Resolves the highest high-side structure anchor from up to 4 supplied pivot records
// @param lookback Number of recent same-side records to scan. Common values: 1, 2, or 4
// @param p1 Most recent price
// @param c1 Most recent close
// @param aux1 Most recent auxiliary value, such as RSI
// @param i1 Most recent pivot bar_index
// @param ci1 Most recent confirmation bar_index
// @returns Selected price, close, auxiliary value, pivot index, confirmation index
export structureResolveHighAnchorFrom4(
     int lookback,
     float p1, float c1, float aux1, int i1, int ci1,
     float p2, float c2, float aux2, int i2, int ci2,
     float p3, float c3, float aux3, int i3, int ci3,
     float p4, float c4, float aux4, int i4, int ci4) =>

    float anchorPrice = p1
    float anchorClose = c1
    float anchorAux = aux1
    int anchorIdx = i1
    int anchorConfirmIdx = ci1

    if lookback >= 2 and not na(p2) and (na(anchorPrice) or p2 > anchorPrice)
        anchorPrice := p2
        anchorClose := c2
        anchorAux := aux2
        anchorIdx := i2
        anchorConfirmIdx := ci2

    if lookback >= 3 and not na(p3) and (na(anchorPrice) or p3 > anchorPrice)
        anchorPrice := p3
        anchorClose := c3
        anchorAux := aux3
        anchorIdx := i3
        anchorConfirmIdx := ci3

    if lookback >= 4 and not na(p4) and (na(anchorPrice) or p4 > anchorPrice)
        anchorPrice := p4
        anchorClose := c4
        anchorAux := aux4
        anchorIdx := i4
        anchorConfirmIdx := ci4

    [anchorPrice, anchorClose, anchorAux, anchorIdx, anchorConfirmIdx]

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Low-Side Anchor Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Resolves the lowest low-side structure anchor from up to 4 supplied pivot records
// @param lookback Number of recent same-side records to scan. Common values: 1, 2, or 4
// @param p1 Most recent price
// @param c1 Most recent close
// @param aux1 Most recent auxiliary value, such as RSI
// @param i1 Most recent pivot bar_index
// @param ci1 Most recent confirmation bar_index
// @returns Selected price, close, auxiliary value, pivot index, confirmation index
export structureResolveLowAnchorFrom4(
     int lookback,
     float p1, float c1, float aux1, int i1, int ci1,
     float p2, float c2, float aux2, int i2, int ci2,
     float p3, float c3, float aux3, int i3, int ci3,
     float p4, float c4, float aux4, int i4, int ci4) =>

    float anchorPrice = p1
    float anchorClose = c1
    float anchorAux = aux1
    int anchorIdx = i1
    int anchorConfirmIdx = ci1

    if lookback >= 2 and not na(p2) and (na(anchorPrice) or p2 < anchorPrice)
        anchorPrice := p2
        anchorClose := c2
        anchorAux := aux2
        anchorIdx := i2
        anchorConfirmIdx := ci2

    if lookback >= 3 and not na(p3) and (na(anchorPrice) or p3 < anchorPrice)
        anchorPrice := p3
        anchorClose := c3
        anchorAux := aux3
        anchorIdx := i3
        anchorConfirmIdx := ci3

    if lookback >= 4 and not na(p4) and (na(anchorPrice) or p4 < anchorPrice)
        anchorPrice := p4
        anchorClose := c4
        anchorAux := aux4
        anchorIdx := i4
        anchorConfirmIdx := ci4

    [anchorPrice, anchorClose, anchorAux, anchorIdx, anchorConfirmIdx]

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Pivot Structure Anchor Resolution Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Pivot Structure Anchor Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable helpers for storing and resolving confirmed pivot
//     structure anchors from synchronized pivot-record arrays.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     This region helps scripts:
//
//     • keep confirmed-pivot memory script-level
//     • store confirmed high-side and low-side pivot records in synchronized arrays
//     • trim those arrays to a controlled maximum length
//     • resolve the highest high-side anchor from a user-defined recent lookback
//     • resolve the lowest low-side anchor from a user-defined recent lookback
//     • carry the selected anchor's matching close, auxiliary value, pivot index,
//       and confirmation index forward with the selected price
//
// 📘 INTERPRETATION:
//     • These helpers are engine-agnostic.
//     • They do not confirm pivots.
//     • They do not decide what qualifies as a pivot.
//     • The calling script supplies already-confirmed pivot records.
//     • The auxiliary value can be RSI, another oscillator, a score, or any other
//       value the script wants attached to the selected anchor.
//
// 📎 NOTES:
//     • Arrays are expected to be synchronized.
//     • The newest record is expected to be at the end of each array.
//     • Ties keep the most recent matching record because the resolver initializes
//       from the newest record and only replaces on a strictly higher/lower value.
//
// ==============================================================================================

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Anchor Record Array Trim Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

_structureTrimFloatArray(array<float> arr, int maxKeep) =>
    while array.size(arr) > maxKeep
        array.shift(arr)

    array.size(arr)

_structureTrimIntArray(array<int> arr, int maxKeep) =>
    while array.size(arr) > maxKeep
        array.shift(arr)

    array.size(arr)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Anchor Record Push Helper
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Pushes one confirmed pivot record into synchronized arrays and trims them to maxRecords
// @param prices Array of pivot prices
// @param closes Array of pivot-close values
// @param auxValues Array of auxiliary values, such as RSI
// @param pivotIdxs Array of pivot bar indexes
// @param confirmIdxs Array of confirmation bar indexes
// @param price New pivot price
// @param closeValue New pivot-close value
// @param auxValue New auxiliary value
// @param pivotIdx New pivot bar_index
// @param confirmIdx New confirmation bar_index
// @param maxRecords Maximum number of records to keep
// @returns Current number of stored price records after trimming
export structurePushAnchorRecord(
     array<float> prices,
     array<float> closes,
     array<float> auxValues,
     array<int> pivotIdxs,
     array<int> confirmIdxs,
     float price,
     float closeValue,
     float auxValue,
     int pivotIdx,
     int confirmIdx,
     int maxRecords) =>

    int maxKeep =
         math.max(maxRecords, 1)

    array.push(prices, price)
    array.push(closes, closeValue)
    array.push(auxValues, auxValue)
    array.push(pivotIdxs, pivotIdx)
    array.push(confirmIdxs, confirmIdx)

    _structureTrimFloatArray(prices, maxKeep)
    _structureTrimFloatArray(closes, maxKeep)
    _structureTrimFloatArray(auxValues, maxKeep)
    _structureTrimIntArray(pivotIdxs, maxKeep)
    _structureTrimIntArray(confirmIdxs, maxKeep)

    array.size(prices)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Anchor Record Array Size Helper
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

_structureRecordArraySize(
     array<float> prices,
     array<float> closes,
     array<float> auxValues,
     array<int> pivotIdxs,
     array<int> confirmIdxs) =>

    int sizeA =
         math.min(array.size(prices), array.size(closes))

    int sizeB =
         math.min(array.size(auxValues), array.size(pivotIdxs))

    math.min(sizeA, math.min(sizeB, array.size(confirmIdxs)))

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Shared Array Anchor Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

_structureResolveAnchorFromArrays(
     array<float> prices,
     array<float> closes,
     array<float> auxValues,
     array<int> pivotIdxs,
     array<int> confirmIdxs,
     int lookback,
     bool isHigh) =>

    int recordCount =
         _structureRecordArraySize(prices, closes, auxValues, pivotIdxs, confirmIdxs)

    float anchorPrice = na
    float anchorClose = na
    float anchorAux = na
    int anchorIdx = na
    int anchorConfirmIdx = na

    if recordCount > 0
        int scanCount =
             math.min(math.max(lookback, 1), recordCount)

        int latestArrayIdx =
             recordCount - 1

        anchorPrice := array.get(prices, latestArrayIdx)
        anchorClose := array.get(closes, latestArrayIdx)
        anchorAux := array.get(auxValues, latestArrayIdx)
        anchorIdx := array.get(pivotIdxs, latestArrayIdx)
        anchorConfirmIdx := array.get(confirmIdxs, latestArrayIdx)

        if scanCount > 1
            for offset = 1 to scanCount - 1
                int testArrayIdx =
                     latestArrayIdx - offset

                float testPrice =
                     array.get(prices, testArrayIdx)

                bool useTestRecord =
                     not na(testPrice) and
                     (
                         na(anchorPrice) or
                         (isHigh and testPrice > anchorPrice) or
                         (not isHigh and testPrice < anchorPrice)
                     )

                if useTestRecord
                    anchorPrice := testPrice
                    anchorClose := array.get(closes, testArrayIdx)
                    anchorAux := array.get(auxValues, testArrayIdx)
                    anchorIdx := array.get(pivotIdxs, testArrayIdx)
                    anchorConfirmIdx := array.get(confirmIdxs, testArrayIdx)

    [anchorPrice, anchorClose, anchorAux, anchorIdx, anchorConfirmIdx]

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: High-Side Array Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Resolves the highest high-side anchor from synchronized pivot-record arrays
// @param prices Array of high-side pivot prices
// @param closes Array of high-side pivot-close values
// @param auxValues Array of high-side auxiliary values, such as RSI
// @param pivotIdxs Array of high-side pivot bar indexes
// @param confirmIdxs Array of high-side confirmation bar indexes
// @param lookback Number of recent same-side records to scan
// @returns Selected price, close, auxiliary value, pivot index, confirmation index
export structureResolveHighAnchorFromArrays(
     array<float> prices,
     array<float> closes,
     array<float> auxValues,
     array<int> pivotIdxs,
     array<int> confirmIdxs,
     int lookback) =>

    _structureResolveAnchorFromArrays(
         prices,
         closes,
         auxValues,
         pivotIdxs,
         confirmIdxs,
         lookback,
         true)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Low-Side Array Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Resolves the lowest low-side anchor from synchronized pivot-record arrays
// @param prices Array of low-side pivot prices
// @param closes Array of low-side pivot-close values
// @param auxValues Array of low-side auxiliary values, such as RSI
// @param pivotIdxs Array of low-side pivot bar indexes
// @param confirmIdxs Array of low-side confirmation bar indexes
// @param lookback Number of recent same-side records to scan
// @returns Selected price, close, auxiliary value, pivot index, confirmation index
export structureResolveLowAnchorFromArrays(
     array<float> prices,
     array<float> closes,
     array<float> auxValues,
     array<int> pivotIdxs,
     array<int> confirmIdxs,
     int lookback) =>

    _structureResolveAnchorFromArrays(
         prices,
         closes,
         auxValues,
         pivotIdxs,
         confirmIdxs,
         lookback,
         false)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// var array<float> recentHighPrices = array.new<float>()
// var array<float> recentHighCloses = array.new<float>()
// var array<float> recentHighAux = array.new<float>()
// var array<int> recentHighIdxs = array.new<int>()
// var array<int> recentHighConfirmIdxs = array.new<int>()
//
// var array<float> recentLowPrices = array.new<float>()
// var array<float> recentLowCloses = array.new<float>()
// var array<float> recentLowAux = array.new<float>()
// var array<int> recentLowIdxs = array.new<int>()
// var array<int> recentLowConfirmIdxs = array.new<int>()
//
// if highConfirmed
//     PSOutils.structurePushAnchorRecord(
//          recentHighPrices,
//          recentHighCloses,
//          recentHighAux,
//          recentHighIdxs,
//          recentHighConfirmIdxs,
//          highPivotPrice,
//          highPivotClose,
//          highPivotRsi,
//          highPivotIdx,
//          bar_index,
//          50)
//
// if lowConfirmed
//     PSOutils.structurePushAnchorRecord(
//          recentLowPrices,
//          recentLowCloses,
//          recentLowAux,
//          recentLowIdxs,
//          recentLowConfirmIdxs,
//          lowPivotPrice,
//          lowPivotClose,
//          lowPivotRsi,
//          lowPivotIdx,
//          bar_index,
//          50)
//
// [activeHighPrice, activeHighClose, activeHighAux, activeHighIdx, activeHighConfirmIdx] =
//      PSOutils.structureResolveHighAnchorFromArrays(
//          recentHighPrices,
//          recentHighCloses,
//          recentHighAux,
//          recentHighIdxs,
//          recentHighConfirmIdxs,
//          4)
//
// [activeLowPrice, activeLowClose, activeLowAux, activeLowIdx, activeLowConfirmIdx] =
//      PSOutils.structureResolveLowAnchorFromArrays(
//          recentLowPrices,
//          recentLowCloses,
//          recentLowAux,
//          recentLowIdxs,
//          recentLowConfirmIdxs,
//          4)
//
// The final lookback value can be script-controlled or user-controlled.
// For example, 1 uses the most recent same-side anchor only,
// 4 scans the last four confirmed same-side anchors,
// and higher values can support wider expanded structure ranges.

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Pivot Structure Anchor Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Pivot Structure Anchor Box Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable helpers for building top and bottom pivot structure anchor
//     boxes from already-confirmed high / low pivot indexes.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     This region helps scripts:
//
//     • build directional top and bottom anchor-box geometry
//     • choose whether box geometry uses:
//          wick-only extension from the candle body
//          or the full candle body itself
//     • return the live box coordinates needed for:
//          top anchor box
//          bottom anchor box
//
// 📘 INTERPRETATION:
//     • Top pivot structure anchor box:
//          "Wick" mode = upper wick only
//          "Body" mode = candle body only
//
//     • Bottom pivot structure anchor box:
//          "Wick" mode = lower wick only
//          "Body" mode = candle body only
//
//     • In Wick mode:
//          a top box only shows if the anchor candle actually has an upper wick
//          a bottom box only shows if the anchor candle actually has a lower wick
//
// 🧰 OUTPUT OPTIONS:
//     • show / hide state for top box
//     • show / hide state for bottom box
//     • left x for top box
//     • left x for bottom box
//     • shared right x
//     • top / bottom y bounds for both boxes
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Pivot Structure Anchor Box Geometry
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Builds the live geometry for top and bottom pivot structure anchor boxes.
//
// Behavior:
//     • Uses confirmed pivot bar indexes as the anchor candles
//     • Converts those indexes into bars-back offsets
//     • Builds directional geometry:
//
//          Top box:
//              Wick mode -> body top to wick top
//              Body mode -> body bottom to body top
//
//          Bottom box:
//              Wick mode -> wick bottom to body bottom
//              Body mode -> body bottom to body top
//
//     • Right side always projects to the current bar
//
// Notes:
//     • This helper returns geometry only
//     • Scripts remain responsible for:
//          colors
//          border settings
//          fill settings
//     • Box lifecycle can remain script-level or be handled through
//       outlineManageBox()
//

// @function Returns the live geometry for top and bottom pivot structure anchor boxes
// @param highPivotIdx Confirmed high pivot bar_index
// @param lowPivotIdx Confirmed low pivot bar_index
// @param boxAreaMode Box area mode. Expected values: "Wick" or "Body"
// @param openValue Open series
// @param highValue High series
// @param lowValue Low series
// @param closeValue Close series
// @returns showHighBox, showLowBox, highLeftX, lowLeftX, boxRightX, highTopY, highBottomY, lowTopY, lowBottomY
export outlineAnchorBoxGeometry(
     int highPivotIdx,
     int lowPivotIdx,
     simple string boxAreaMode,
     float openValue,
     float highValue,
     float lowValue,
     float closeValue) =>

    bool useWickBoxes =
         boxAreaMode == "Wick"

    int highBoxBA =
         not na(highPivotIdx) ? bar_index - highPivotIdx : na

    int lowBoxBA =
         not na(lowPivotIdx) ? bar_index - lowPivotIdx : na

    bool hasHighAnchor =
         not na(highPivotIdx) and
         not na(highBoxBA) and
         highBoxBA >= 0

    bool hasLowAnchor =
         not na(lowPivotIdx) and
         not na(lowBoxBA) and
         lowBoxBA >= 0

    float highBodyTop =
         hasHighAnchor ? math.max(openValue[highBoxBA], closeValue[highBoxBA]) : na

    float highBodyBottom =
         hasHighAnchor ? math.min(openValue[highBoxBA], closeValue[highBoxBA]) : na

    float lowBodyTop =
         hasLowAnchor ? math.max(openValue[lowBoxBA], closeValue[lowBoxBA]) : na

    float lowBodyBottom =
         hasLowAnchor ? math.min(openValue[lowBoxBA], closeValue[lowBoxBA]) : na

    bool highHasUpperWick =
         hasHighAnchor and
         not na(highBodyTop) and
         highValue[highBoxBA] > highBodyTop

    bool lowHasLowerWick =
         hasLowAnchor and
         not na(lowBodyBottom) and
         lowValue[lowBoxBA] < lowBodyBottom

    bool showHighBox =
         hasHighAnchor and
         (
             not useWickBoxes or
             highHasUpperWick
         )

    bool showLowBox =
         hasLowAnchor and
         (
             not useWickBoxes or
             lowHasLowerWick
         )

    float highTopY =
         showHighBox ?
         (
             useWickBoxes ?
             highValue[highBoxBA] :
             highBodyTop
         ) :
         na

    float highBottomY =
         showHighBox ?
         (
             useWickBoxes ?
             highBodyTop :
             highBodyBottom
         ) :
         na

    float lowTopY =
         showLowBox ?
         (
             useWickBoxes ?
             lowBodyBottom :
             lowBodyTop
         ) :
         na

    float lowBottomY =
         showLowBox ?
         (
             useWickBoxes ?
             lowValue[lowBoxBA] :
             lowBodyBottom
         ) :
         na

    int highLeftX =
         showHighBox ? highPivotIdx : na

    int lowLeftX =
         showLowBox ? lowPivotIdx : na

    int boxRightX =
         bar_index

    [showHighBox, showLowBox, highLeftX, lowLeftX, boxRightX, highTopY, highBottomY, lowTopY, lowBottomY]


// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example usage in a script that imports this library:
//
// import MYNAMEISBRANDON/PivotStructureOutline_Utilities/3 as PSOutils
//
// [showHighBox, showLowBox, highLeftX, lowLeftX, boxRightX, highTopY, highBottomY, lowTopY, lowBottomY] = PSOutils.outlineAnchorBoxGeometry(
//      lastHighPivotIdx,
//      lastLowPivotIdx,
//      in_majorPivotBoxArea,
//      open,
//      high,
//      low,
//      close)
//
// highAnchorBox := PSOutils.outlineManageBox(
//      showHighBox,
//      highAnchorBox,
//      showHighBox ? highLeftX : bar_index,
//      showHighBox ? highTopY : close,
//      showHighBox ? boxRightX : bar_index,
//      showHighBox ? highBottomY : close,
//      highBoxFill,
//      highBoxBorder,
//      in_majorPivotBoxBorderStyle,
//      in_majorPivotBoxBorderWidth)
//
// lowAnchorBox := PSOutils.outlineManageBox(
//      showLowBox,
//      lowAnchorBox,
//      showLowBox ? lowLeftX : bar_index,
//      showLowBox ? lowTopY : close,
//      showLowBox ? boxRightX : bar_index,
//      showLowBox ? lowBottomY : close,
//      lowBoxFill,
//      lowBoxBorder,
//      in_majorPivotBoxBorderStyle,
//      in_majorPivotBoxBorderWidth)

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Pivot Structure Anchor Box Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Active Anchor Marker Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable label-circle helpers for marking active pivot structure
//     anchors on the chart.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     This region helps scripts:
//
//     • convert a simple UI-facing size string into a Pine label size enum
//     • create, update, or delete small circle labels at active structure anchors
//     • mark only the currently resolved high-side / low-side anchors
//     • keep marker lifecycle logic consistent across outline-based scripts
//
// 📘 INTERPRETATION:
//     • These helpers do not choose which anchor should be active.
//     • These helpers do not decide marker colors.
//     • These helpers do not resolve structure tags.
//     • The calling script supplies:
//          enabled state
//          x/y anchor location
//          marker color
//          marker size
//
// 📎 NOTES:
//     • This uses label.style_circle, not plotshape().
//     • That makes it suitable for last-bar managed active-anchor markers.
//     • Historical pivot markers can still be handled at script level with
//       plotshape() when a script wants to mark every confirmed pivot.
//
// ==============================================================================================

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Active Anchor Marker Size Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Converts a simple size string into a Pine label size enum.
//
// Behavior:
//     • "Tiny"   -> size.tiny
//     • "Small"  -> size.small
//     • "Large"  -> size.large
//     • "Huge"   -> size.huge
//     • fallback -> size.normal
//
// @function Resolves a Pine label size from a string input for active anchor markers
// @param sizeIn Size string. Expected values: "Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", or "Huge"
// @returns Pine label size enum
export outlineMarkerSize(simple string sizeIn) =>
    sizeIn == "Tiny" ? size.tiny :
     sizeIn == "Small" ? size.small :
     sizeIn == "Large" ? size.large :
     sizeIn == "Huge" ? size.huge :
     size.normal

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Active Anchor Circle Label Manager
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Creates, updates, or deletes a small circle label at an active structure anchor.
//
// Behavior:
//     • If enabled and the label does not exist, creates it
//     • If enabled and the label already exists, updates its location, color, and size
//     • If disabled and the label exists, deletes it
//     • Uses xloc.bar_index and yloc.price
//     • Uses label.style_circle with empty text
//
// Notes:
//     • Good fit for active high/low structure-anchor markers.
//     • The calling script remains responsible for deciding:
//          whether the marker should show
//          which x/y anchor to use
//          which color to apply
//
// @function Creates, updates, or deletes an active anchor circle label
// @param lbl Existing label reference
// @param enabled Whether the marker should exist
// @param x Anchor bar_index
// @param y Anchor price
// @param markerColor Circle color
// @param markerSize Pine label size enum
// @returns Updated label reference
export outlineManageCircleLabel(
     label lbl,
     bool enabled,
     int x,
     float y,
     color markerColor,
     string markerSize) =>

    label out =
         lbl

    if enabled and not na(x) and not na(y)
        if na(out)
            out := label.new(
                 x=x,
                 y=y,
                 text="",
                 xloc=xloc.bar_index,
                 yloc=yloc.price,
                 style=label.style_circle,
                 color=markerColor,
                 size=markerSize)
        else
            label.set_xy(out, x, y)
            label.set_color(out, markerColor)
            label.set_size(out, markerSize)
    else
        if not na(out)
            label.delete(out)
            out := na

    out

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// var label activeHighMarker = na
// var label activeLowMarker = na
//
// if barstate.islast
//     string markerSize = PSOutils.outlineMarkerSize("Tiny")
//
//     activeHighMarker := PSOutils.outlineManageCircleLabel(
//          activeHighMarker,
//          showHighMarker,
//          highAnchorIdx,
//          highAnchorY,
//          highMarkerColor,
//          markerSize)
//
//     activeLowMarker := PSOutils.outlineManageCircleLabel(
//          activeLowMarker,
//          showLowMarker,
//          lowAnchorIdx,
//          lowAnchorY,
//          lowMarkerColor,
//          markerSize)

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Active Anchor Marker Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Pivot Structure AVWAP Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable AVWAP helpers for scripts that want to draw AVWAP paths
//     from already-resolved pivot structure anchors.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     This region helps scripts:
//
//     • build AVWAP chart-point paths from cumulative price-volume and volume
//     • keep AVWAP point-builder calls in global scope while safely gating work
//     • cap the visible AVWAP draw window without changing the true anchor math
//     • create, delete, and recreate AVWAP polylines from active point arrays
//
// 📘 INTERPRETATION:
//     • These helpers do not confirm pivots.
//     • These helpers do not choose which anchor should be active.
//     • These helpers do not decide whether a script shows:
//          Backfilled Pivot-Bar AVWAP
//          Confirmation-Bar AVWAP
//          high-side AVWAP
//          low-side AVWAP
//     • The calling script supplies:
//          cumulative PV
//          cumulative volume
//          anchor index
//          draw-start index
//          end index
//          display state
//          colors / widths / styles
//
// 📎 NOTES:
//     • The true AVWAP anchor remains the supplied anchor index.
//     • The draw-start index only controls how much of the AVWAP path is visible.
//     • structureManageAvwapPolyline() deletes and recreates the polyline, so it
//       is intended for last-bar render workflows.
//     • This keeps the helper engine-agnostic and compatible with pivot, RSI,
//       oscillator, zone, or other structure-based scripts.
//
// ==============================================================================================

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: AVWAP Safe Anchor Helper
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Returns a safe anchor index only when the AVWAP should be built on the
//     last bar.
//
// Behavior:
//     • Returns anchorIdx when enabled, on the last bar, and anchorIdx is valid.
//     • Returns na otherwise.
//     • This lets scripts keep AVWAP point-builder calls in global scope while
//       avoiding expensive point construction across historical bars.
//
// @function Returns a last-bar-safe AVWAP anchor index
// @param enabled Whether this AVWAP path should be active
// @param anchorIdx True AVWAP anchor bar_index
// @returns Safe anchor index or na
export structureAvwapSafeAnchorIdx(
     bool enabled,
     int anchorIdx) =>

    enabled and barstate.islast and not na(anchorIdx) ? anchorIdx : na

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: AVWAP Draw Start Helper
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Resolves the visible AVWAP start index while preserving the true anchor.
//
// Behavior:
//     • If safeAnchorIdx exists, the visible start is capped to maxDrawBars.
//     • The returned value controls only the visible point path.
//     • It does not change where the AVWAP math is anchored.
//
// @function Resolves a capped visible AVWAP draw-start index
// @param safeAnchorIdx Last-bar-safe AVWAP anchor index
// @param maxDrawBars Maximum number of bars to draw backward from the current bar
// @returns Visible AVWAP start index or na
export structureAvwapDrawStartIdx(
     int safeAnchorIdx,
     int maxDrawBars) =>

    not na(safeAnchorIdx)
     ? math.max(safeAnchorIdx, bar_index - math.max(maxDrawBars, 1))
     : na

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: AVWAP Point Builder
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Builds chart points for an AVWAP path from cumulative PV and cumulative volume.
//
// Behavior:
//     • Uses anchorIdx as the true AVWAP anchor.
//     • Uses startIdx and endIdx as the visible draw window.
//     • Reconstructs each visible AVWAP point from cumulative PV / volume.
//     • Returns an empty point array when inputs are invalid.
//
// Notes:
//     • cumPV should usually be ta.cum(source * volume).
//     • cumVol should usually be ta.cum(volume).
//     • This helper works for both:
//          Pivot-Bar AVWAP
//          Confirmation-Bar AVWAP
//       because the caller decides which anchorIdx to pass.
//
// @function Builds AVWAP chart points from cumulative PV / volume series
// @param cumPV Cumulative price-volume series
// @param cumVol Cumulative volume series
// @param anchorIdx True AVWAP anchor bar_index
// @param startIdx Visible draw-start bar_index
// @param endIdx Visible draw-end bar_index
// @returns Array of chart points for polyline rendering
export structureAvwapPointsFromCum(
     float cumPV,
     float cumVol,
     int anchorIdx,
     int startIdx,
     int endIdx) =>

    array<chart.point> pts =
         array.new<chart.point>()

    int anchorBarsBack =
         not na(anchorIdx) ? bar_index - anchorIdx : na

    float pvBeforeAnchor =
         not na(anchorBarsBack) and anchorBarsBack >= 0 ? nz(cumPV[anchorBarsBack + 1]) : na

    float volBeforeAnchor =
         not na(anchorBarsBack) and anchorBarsBack >= 0 ? nz(cumVol[anchorBarsBack + 1]) : na

    if not na(anchorIdx) and not na(startIdx) and not na(endIdx) and startIdx <= endIdx
        for x = startIdx to endIdx
            int barsBackX =
                 bar_index - x

            float pvAtX =
                 barsBackX >= 0 ? cumPV[barsBackX] : na

            float volAtX =
                 barsBackX >= 0 ? cumVol[barsBackX] : na

            float pvSpanAtX =
                 not na(pvAtX) and not na(pvBeforeAnchor) ? pvAtX - pvBeforeAnchor : na

            float volSpanAtX =
                 not na(volAtX) and not na(volBeforeAnchor) ? volAtX - volBeforeAnchor : na

            float y =
                 not na(volSpanAtX) and volSpanAtX > 0 ? pvSpanAtX / volSpanAtX : na

            if not na(y)
                array.push(pts, chart.point.from_index(x, y))

    pts

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: AVWAP Polyline Manager
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Deletes and recreates an AVWAP polyline from the supplied point array.
//
// Behavior:
//     • Deletes the previous polyline if one exists.
//     • Creates a new polyline only when enabled and at least 2 points exist.
//     • Uses xloc.bar_index.
//     • Uses force_overlay=true so price-pane AVWAP paths render on the chart.
//
// Notes:
//     • This is intended for barstate.islast render blocks.
//     • The caller controls colors, width, and line style.
//     • lineStyle should already be a Pine line-style enum, commonly resolved
//       through outlineLineStyle().
//
// @function Deletes and recreates an AVWAP polyline from chart points
// @param pl Existing polyline reference
// @param enabled Whether the polyline should exist
// @param pts Array of chart points to draw
// @param lineColor Polyline color
// @param lineWidth Polyline width
// @param lineStyle Pine line style enum
// @returns Updated polyline reference
export structureManageAvwapPolyline(
     polyline pl,
     bool enabled,
     array<chart.point> pts,
     color lineColor,
     int lineWidth,
     string lineStyle) =>

    polyline out =
         pl

    if not na(out)
        polyline.delete(out)
        out := na

    if enabled and array.size(pts) >= 2
        out := polyline.new(
             pts,
             curved=false,
             closed=false,
             xloc=xloc.bar_index,
             line_color=lineColor,
             fill_color=na,
             line_style=lineStyle,
             line_width=lineWidth,
             force_overlay=true)

    out

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// float cumPV = ta.cum(hlc3 * volume)
// float cumVol = ta.cum(volume)
//
// int safeAnchor = PSOutils.structureAvwapSafeAnchorIdx(
//      showAvwap,
//      structurePivotIdx)
//
// int drawStart = PSOutils.structureAvwapDrawStartIdx(
//      safeAnchor,
//      500)
//
// array<chart.point> avwapPts = PSOutils.structureAvwapPointsFromCum(
//      cumPV,
//      cumVol,
//      safeAnchor,
//      drawStart,
//      bar_index)
//
// var polyline avwapPoly = na
//
// if barstate.islast
//     avwapPoly := PSOutils.structureManageAvwapPolyline(
//          avwapPoly,
//          showAvwap,
//          avwapPts,
//          color.new(color.orange, 0),
//          2,
//          line.style_solid)

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Pivot Structure AVWAP Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Line Object Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable line-object lifecycle helpers for scripts using the
//     Pivot Structure Outline utilities library.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     This region helps scripts:
//
//     • create a line when it should exist
//     • update an existing line in place as geometry changes
//     • delete a line when it should no longer exist
//
// 📎 NOTES:
//     • Geometry still comes from the script or from other exported helpers
//     • This helper only manages the live line object itself
//
// ==============================================================================================

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Line Object Manager
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Creates, updates, or deletes a line object using supplied geometry.
//
// Behavior:
//     • If enabled and the line does not exist, creates it
//     • If enabled and the line already exists, updates it in place
//     • If disabled and the line exists, deletes it
//     • Uses xloc.bar_index and extend.none
//
// Notes:
//     • Good fit for live last-bar line rendering
//     • Keeps line lifecycle logic consistent across scripts
//     • Line style is expected to already be resolved by the caller
//

// @function Creates, updates, or deletes a line object
// @param enabled Whether the line should exist
// @param ln Existing line reference
// @param x1 Start x position
// @param y1 Start y position
// @param x2 End x position
// @param y2 End y position
// @param col Line color
// @param width Line width
// @param style Line style
// @returns Updated line reference
export outlineManageLine(
     bool enabled,
     line ln,
     int x1,
     float y1,
     int x2,
     float y2,
     color col,
     int width,
     string style) =>

    line out = ln

    if enabled
        if na(out)
            out := line.new(
                 x1=x1,
                 y1=y1,
                 x2=x2,
                 y2=y2,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_index,
                 extend=extend.none,
                 color=col,
                 width=width,
                 style=style)
        else
            line.set_xy1(out, x1, y1)
            line.set_xy2(out, x2, y2)
            line.set_color(out, col)
            line.set_width(out, width)
            line.set_style(out, style)
    else
        if not na(out)
            line.delete(out)
            out := na

    out

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// outlineHighLine := PSOutils.outlineManageLine(
//      enableHighLine,
//      outlineHighLine,
//      enableHighLine ? outlineLeftX : bar_index,
//      enableHighLine ? outlineTopY : close,
//      enableHighLine ? outlineRightX : bar_index,
//      enableHighLine ? outlineTopY : close,
//      outlineColor,
//      in_outlineWidth,
//      PSOutils.outlineLineStyle(in_outlineStyle))

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Line Object Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Box Object Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable box-object lifecycle helpers for scripts using the
//     Pivot Structure Outline utilities library.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     This region helps scripts:
//
//     • create a box when it should exist
//     • update an existing box in place as geometry changes
//     • delete a box when it should no longer exist
//
// 📎 NOTES:
//     • Geometry still comes from the script or from other exported helpers
//     • This helper only manages the live box object itself
//
// ==============================================================================================

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Box Object Manager
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Purpose:
//     Creates, updates, or deletes a box object using supplied geometry.
//
// Behavior:
//     • If enabled and the box does not exist, creates it
//     • If enabled and the box already exists, updates it in place
//     • If disabled and the box exists, deletes it
//
// Notes:
//     • Good fit for live last-bar box rendering
//     • Keeps box lifecycle logic consistent across scripts
//

// @function Creates, updates, or deletes a box object
// @param enabled Whether the box should exist
// @param bx Existing box reference
// @param left Left x position
// @param top Top y position
// @param right Right x position
// @param bottom Bottom y position
// @param bgColor Box background color
// @param borderColor Box border color
// @param borderStyle Box border style
// @param borderWidth Box border width
// @returns Updated box reference
export outlineManageBox(
     bool enabled,
     box bx,
     int left,
     float top,
     int right,
     float bottom,
     color bgColor,
     color borderColor,
     string borderStyle,
     int borderWidth) =>

    box out = bx

    string resolvedBorderStyle =
         outlineLineStyle(borderStyle)

    if enabled
        if na(out)
            out := box.new(
                 left=left,
                 top=top,
                 right=right,
                 bottom=bottom,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_index,
                 bgcolor=bgColor,
                 border_color=borderColor,
                 border_style=resolvedBorderStyle,
                 border_width=borderWidth)
        else
            box.set_left(out, left)
            box.set_top(out, top)
            box.set_right(out, right)
            box.set_bottom(out, bottom)
            box.set_bgcolor(out, bgColor)
            box.set_border_color(out, borderColor)
            box.set_border_style(out, resolvedBorderStyle)
            box.set_border_width(out, borderWidth)
    else
        if not na(out)
            box.delete(out)
            out := na

    out

